# Mutation sanity check — issue-22-qa-v1 (bed330e)

Purpose: confirm the Builder's guard tests can fail (no test that only asserts on
its own mock). Two mutants applied locally to src/ai/CLIPresets.ts, suite re-run,
then restored with `git checkout --`. No mutation reached a commit.

## Mutant 1 — drop the defaultProvider override precedence

Change: `const forced = wanted && wanted !== 'auto' ? wanted : undefined;`
     → `const forced = undefined as string | undefined;`
   (selectCLICommand ignores aiCodeReview.cli.defaultProvider entirely)

Result (node --test src/test/node/cliPresets.cjs):

    not ok 10 - defaultProvider setting overrides a stale persisted pick; auto keeps it
    # tests 14
    # pass 12
    # fail 1

Killed by: "defaultProvider setting overrides a stale persisted pick; auto keeps it".
Restored → green.

## Mutant 2 — drop the switcher persistence write

Change: removed `await options.save(picked);` from switchCLIProvider
   (switch no longer persists the picked provider)

Result (node --test src/test/node/cliPresets.cjs):

    not ok 11 - switcher persists the picked provider and the next run uses it silently
    not ok 12 - switcher reflects a concrete setting, rewrites it on switch, lists a not-found forced provider
    # tests 14
    # pass 11
    # fail 2

Killed by: the persistence test (AC1) and the setting-rewrite test (AC2).
Restored → `# pass 13 # fail 0` (13 pass + 1 Windows-only skip).

## Surviving-mutant note

`>` → `>=` class mutants in the `settingForced !== picked` guard (line 159) are
not pinned: switching to the same provider as the forced setting writes the
persisted pick but skips the setting rewrite. No test covers pick === forced
setting. Ranked Low (no observable behavior difference — setting already equals
the pick); listed in the QA handoff under "Test gaps (not written)".
